  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Town list status Complete; 3 below-market units. Council took up the plan on 2026-08-11 and voted to revisit it in October; no later outcome found.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001555"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Applicant letter: 12 units, 9 single-family homes of about 5,775 to 6,170 sq ft and 3 detached row house units of about 1,630 sq ft, on a private road. Zoned Resource Conservation; General Plan Agriculture; Williamson Act contract terminated January 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004022",
        "SRC-004021"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Applicant letter: the Surrey Farms neighborhood was laid out by Bob Dodge in the 1950s; his children Tom, Linda and Larry are pursuing this final phase.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004022"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CEQAnet: 11 residences on the western slope plus one on Lot 10 on the northeastern slope; lots about 0.1 to 5.48 acres; eastern portion left undeveloped; access from Twin Oaks Drive and, for Lot 10, Cerro Vista Court.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004021"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Los Gatan (2026-06-17): plan floor area changed from 62,000 to 90,000 sq ft after an error was found; Planning Commission vote 4-1, Burnett opposed. The Town pending projects page lists Planning Commission verbatim minutes dated 2026-06-11.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004024",
        "SRC-004023"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Los Gatan (2026-09-02): at the 2026-08-11 special meeting Council asked for more information on whether an EIR is required instead of an MND and voted to revisit the project in October.",
